@startuml owner-dependency-graph
!include _theme.iuml

start

:Collect every owner-level change
the plan produced;

:Record what each one waits for;
note right
  A change carries its prerequisites.
  Nothing infers them from the order
  the file happens to be written in.
end note

if (Does anything wait for a change
that is not in this run?) then (yes)
  :Report it as blocked;
  note right
    A parent that already exists is
    nothing to wait for. A parent that
    was never declared is a mistake in
    the file, and is named as one.
  end note
  stop
else (no)
endif

repeat
  :Take the changes whose prerequisites
  have all succeeded;
  :Attempt them;

  if (Did a prerequisite fail?) then (yes)
    :Block everything that waited for it;
    note right
      Blocked, not attempted. Sending a
      child team to sit under a parent
      that does not exist would fail in a
      way nobody asked about.
    end note
  else (no)
  endif
repeat while (Anything left that can be attempted?) is (yes)
->no;

:Report every outcome, including the
ones that were never attempted;

stop
@enduml
